questions.explanation:
Given:

&ang;P = 75&ordm;

The internal bisectors of &ang;Q and &ang;R meet at S.

Formula used:

Sum of angles in a triangle: &ang;P + &ang;Q + &ang;R = 180&ordm;

Angle formed by the intersection of two angle bisectors:

&ang;QSR = 90&ordm; + (&ang;P / 2)

Calculation:

Calculate &ang;Q + &ang;R:

&ang;P + &ang;Q + &ang;R = 180&ordm;

75&ordm; + &ang;Q + &ang;R = 180&ordm;

&ang;Q + &ang;R = 105&ordm;

Calculate &ang;QSR:

&ang;QSR = 90&ordm; + (75&ordm; / 2)

&ang;QSR = 90&ordm; + 37.5&ordm;

&ang;QSR = 127.5&ordm;

**&there4; m&ang;QSR = 127.5&ordm;.**

questions.explanationHi:
दिया गया है:

&ang;P = 75&deg;

&ang;Q और &ang;R के आंतरिक समद्विभाजक बिंदु S पर मिलते हैं।

प्रयुक्त सूत्र:

त्रिभुज के कोणों का योग: &ang;P + &ang;Q + &ang;R = 180&deg;

दो कोण समद्विभाजकों के प्रतिच्छेदन से बना कोण:

&ang;QSR = 90&deg; + (&ang;P / 2)

गणना:

&ang;Q + &ang;R की गणना करें:

&ang;P + &ang;Q + &ang;R = 180&deg;

75&deg; + &ang;Q + &ang;R = 180&deg;

&ang;Q + &ang;R = 105&deg;

&ang;QSR की गणना करें:

&ang;QSR = 90&deg; + (75&deg; / 2)

&ang;QSR = 90&deg; + 37.5&deg;

&ang;QSR = 127.5&deg;

**इसलिए m&ang;QSR = 127.5&deg;।**
